\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Comparison with a continuum covariance}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{For a supplied operator #{C} as in \ref{fdip-01DY},
the continuum notation #{C=(\mu -\covdot K\cov)^{-1}}
records its Fourier multipliers on the unit torus with coordinate
volume. The factors #{B^n} in the test functions make
\ref{fdip-01DY} a comparison of means rather than unnormalized
integrals. The comparison concerns a deterministic operator
pairing; a random field realizing it is a separate construction.}

\p{In dimensions #{n\ge2}, the tested covariances do not
assert finite pointwise field values or a pointwise convergent
Green-function expansion. The coherent box probability in
\ref{fdip-01D7} is already constructed from finite Gaussian
limits and their consistency under merging.}
